# Orel-Who-Did-Not-Grow — swamp T2 basic duelist (flesh-mutant child)

[title Orel-Who-Did-Not-Grow]
[image monsters/swamp_child.png]
[blood #3a3024]
[stats hp=18]

* move Attack
  narration: It darts in low and bites down on whatever it reaches.
  narration: It snatches at your sleeve with a hand that ends a finger short.

* move Defend
  narration: It crouches and the wet ribs flex inward, sheltering the soft places.

* move Recover
  narration: It goes very still on the planks. Whatever it lost, the swamp gives back.

* move Venomous Heavy Slow Attack
  narration: It throws itself into you and clings, biting where it can hold, the mouth opening further than it should.

* move Heavy Power Defend
  narration: It folds itself smaller than a child has any right to fold, the joints in the wrong order.

* intro
It is on the plank walkway ahead, crouched, watching. The shape is a
child's shape, mostly. The ribs show through the wet skin in places they
should not, and one arm ends a finger short. It does not move when you
approach. It does not move when you stop. Then it stands, all wrong, the
joints in the wrong order, and begins to come toward you in the gait of
something that has never been told it is not a child. You remember, too
late to matter now, hearing that you should offer it food.

* win
+give_gold 10
+add_tag killed_orel
It folds on the planks with a small wet sound and does not get up. The
walkway holds it the way the walkway holds anything else. You step
around it carefully and keep moving, and try not to think about whose
child it had once been, or whether anyone had told its mother.

* lose
The mouth opens further than it should. The walkway holds you the way
the walkway holds anything else.
